# Deliberately empty. `wrangler types` reads `.dev.vars` by default and folds
# whatever it finds into the generated `Env`, so the committed
# `worker-configuration.d.ts` depended on whether the person regenerating it
# happened to have a local `.dev.vars` — and CI, which has none, then failed
# `wrangler types --check`.
#
# `--env-file` REPLACES that default, so pointing it at this file makes
# generation identical everywhere. The Worker secrets it used to pick up
# (OIDC_CLIENT_SECRET, SESSION_SECRET, DATABASE_URL) are declared by hand in
# `app/server/env.d.ts`, which is where they belong: they are secrets, not
# wrangler `vars`, so they should never have come from a local file.
